      "range": [
        "spya-s2680p",
        "spya-taz7j0"
      ],
      "title": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland",
      "gist": "Modern work, despite its flaws, gives people impersonal respect and independence that relational societies cannot, which is why losing it to AI would be a real loss, not a gain.",
      "question": "work and dignity — why does modern work matter for respect and freedom beyond just paying the bills? (a historical argument)",
      "sourceHeading": "Friendship was invented in 18th-century Scotland"
    },
    "n0089": {
      "id": "n0089",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0088",
      "children": [
